  "question": "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1\\\\2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $B=2A$.<br><br><b>(a)</b> Find $\\operatorname{adj}A$ and $A^{-1}$.<br><br><b>(b)</b> Determine $\\operatorname{adj}B$ and $B^{-1}$.<br><br><b>(c)</b> Compare $B^{-1}$ with $A^{-1}$ and establish the relation between them.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "<b>(a)</b><br>For<br>$$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1\\\\2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>$$|A|=4(3)-1(2)=10$$<br>Therefore,<br>$$\\operatorname{adj}A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\\\-2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>and<br>$$A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\\\-2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><br><b>(b)</b><br>Since $B=2A$,<br>$$B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2\\\\4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Therefore,<br>$$\\operatorname{adj}B=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2\\\\-4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}=2\\operatorname{adj}A$$<br>Also,<br>$$|B|=8(6)-2(4)=40$$<br>Hence,<br>$$B^{-1}=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2\\\\-4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\\\-2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><br><b>(c)</b><br>Since<br>$$A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\\\-2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>and<br>$$B^{-1}=\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\\\-2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>we obtain<br>$$B^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}A^{-1}$$<br>Thus, $(2A)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}A^{-1}$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "(a) $\\operatorname{adj}A=\\begin{bmatrix}3&-1\\\\-2&4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}3&-1\\\\-2&4\\end{bmatrix}$<br>(b) $\\operatorname{adj}B=\\begin{bmatrix}6&-2\\\\-4&8\\end{bmatrix}=2\\operatorname{adj}A$ and $B^{-1}=\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}3&-1\\\\-2&4\\end{bmatrix}$<br>(c) $B^{-1}=\\frac12A^{-1}$",
    "B": "(a) $A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{adj}A$<br>(b) $\\operatorname{adj}B=4\\operatorname{adj}A$ and $B^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{adj}A$<br>(c) $B^{-1}=A^{-1}$",
    "C": "(a) $\\operatorname{adj}A=\\begin{bmatrix}4&-1\\\\-2&3\\end{bmatrix}$<br>(b) $\\operatorname{adj}B=\\operatorname{adj}A$<br>(c) $B^{-1}=2A^{-1}$",
